# ffgithubrunners secrets — copied to ~/.config/ffgithubrunners/secrets.env at mode 0600 by
# 04-github.sh, and owned by the account that runs the supervisor. NO CONTAINER EVER SEES THIS
# FILE: it is read by the supervisor on the host, and only the minted JIT config crosses into a
# container.
#
# This is the ONLY credential this system holds. The Unity and GitHub secrets a job uses reach it
# from the workflow's env: block, out of repository secrets, exactly as they do today.
#
# Fill in ONE of the two blocks below.

# --- Option A: a fine-grained PAT ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The smallest thing that works. One setting to create: a fine-grained personal access token
# scoped to the Final-Factory organization, with
#
#     Organization permissions -> Self-hosted runners -> Read and write
#
# It is a personal credential and does not expire on its own, which is the argument for Option B.
#FFGHR_GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# --- Option B: a GitHub App ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Better hygiene: installation tokens expire in an hour and no personal account is in the loop.
# Create an App on the organization with the same Self-hosted runners: Read and write permission,
# install it on Final-Factory, download a private key, and put the .pem beside this file at 0600.
#
# The app id is on the App's settings page. The installation id is in the URL when you open
# Settings -> Applications -> the App -> Configure:
#   https://github.com/organizations/Final-Factory/settings/installations/<INSTALLATION ID>
#FFGHR_APP_ID=123456
#FFGHR_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=98765432
#FFGHR_APP_KEY=/home/FinalFactoryTester/.config/ffgithubrunners/github-app.pem
